  <h2 id="trends">Use trend-led design as a collection refresh, not a gamble</h2>
  <p>
    Trend-led activewear does not require replacing the entire core collection. A new neckline, contrast trim, refined neutral, seasonal color, capri proportion, tennis skirt or sculpting layer can give a familiar category a fresh point of view. The strongest collections pair these updates with styles that already make sense for the customer’s routine.
  </p>
  <p>
    For a smaller first buy, use a conservative color base and place trend exposure in a limited number of styles. This allows a buyer to learn what customers respond to before committing to a broader custom development program. If the demand is proven, the next step can be a private-label refresh or a deeper OEM/ODM project with more exclusive details.
  </p>

  <h2>Ready stock, private label or custom development?</h2>
  <p>
    The three routes serve different collection goals. A ready-stock selection is useful for speed and product testing. Private label adds more brand presentation to selected existing styles. Custom OEM/ODM makes sense when the brand needs its own fit, fabric, construction or exclusive design direction. A clear catalog request helps identify which route fits each product rather than forcing the whole assortment into one model.
  </p>

  <h2 id="catalog-request">How to request the right ready-stock catalog selection</h2>
  <p>
    A broad request for “all activewear” can slow down a sourcing conversation. Instead, tell us the type of collection you want to build. For example: a Pilates capsule, studio yoga essentials, gym training basics, women’s tennis-inspired sets or a comfort-led travel and athleisure range.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Share your target customer, market and intended product categories.</li>
    <li>State your estimated quantity, preferred colors and size range.</li>
    <li>Tell us whether you need ready stock only, private-label details or a path toward custom development.</li>
    <li>Request current style, fabric, color and size information for the shortlisted products.</li>
    <li>Review samples and document the approved fit, fabric, branding and packaging details before bulk confirmation.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    FITCLO has worked with global activewear buyers since 2010. Send your selection brief and we can help direct you to relevant ready-stock products, practical branding options and the appropriate next step for your collection.
  </p>
